    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The issue is the actual data from the Pacific project. We only saw a 5% increase in coral health. It's way below our 20% target and honestly looks pretty underwhelming on paper. If we just report a 5% increase, I'm worried the Fund will think we're inefficient and pass us over for the $5M. How do we frame that 5% so it doesn't look like a failure and instead makes us look like an organization that's actually winning?",
